WEBVTT

00:00:28.115 --> 00:00:31.994
 <i>'Twas the day before Christmas
Before the Bad Guys turned good</i>

00:00:31.994 --> 00:00:35.623
<i>When all through the city
They cased each and every neighborhood</i>

00:00:35.623 --> 00:00:38.000
Did that rhyme? Is "'twas" even a word?

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:39.668
Look, here's the thing.

00:00:39.668 --> 00:00:42.880
Our story is set
when the Bad Guys were still bad, okay?

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:46.342
And at the best time of the year,
when all the good heists can be had.

00:00:47.009 --> 00:00:49.053
All right, guys, what's tomorrow?

00:00:49.053 --> 00:00:54.433
The Bad Guys
Holiday Heist-tacular!

00:00:54.433 --> 00:00:57.478
 The Bad Guys
Holiday Heist-tacular!

00:00:57.478 --> 00:00:58.521
What does that mean?

00:00:58.521 --> 00:01:02.233
While all these normies stay home
with their loved ones, or whatever...

00:01:02.233 --> 00:01:04.360
...this place turns into a ghost town!

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:05.736
No guards, no fuzz.

00:01:05.736 --> 00:01:08.197
This city's our heisting stage!

00:01:08.197 --> 00:01:10.366
And we're gonna clean it out.

00:01:10.366 --> 00:01:12.243
Oh, it's a Bad Guys tradition.

00:01:12.243 --> 00:01:13.828
And so is spending the day before

00:01:13.828 --> 00:01:17.456
coming up with a list of everything
we're going to steal Christmas morning.

00:01:17.456 --> 00:01:20.292
Ooh, I want to hit that place
with all the stinky cheese.

00:01:20.292 --> 00:01:22.086
No reason. I-I don't even like it.

00:01:23.212 --> 00:01:26.173
- Okay, I like it a little!
- Cheesy Dan's is on the list.

00:01:32.805 --> 00:01:35.599
City... Corporate... Bank.

00:01:36.141 --> 00:01:39.103
Oh, yeah. That's what we've been waiting
all year for.

00:01:39.103 --> 00:01:42.565
It's gonna be the cherry
on top of our criminal sundae.

00:01:42.565 --> 00:01:43.983
Tomorrow morning, it,

00:01:43.983 --> 00:01:46.694
and everything else in this city,
will be ours.

00:01:46.694 --> 00:01:49.071
-  That's what I'm talking about!

00:01:53.409 --> 00:01:56.412
Tiffany Fluffit here with
the moment we've all been waiting for.

00:01:56.412 --> 00:02:00.082
Our beloved Big Nick
has just made his first appearance.

00:02:00.082 --> 00:02:03.419
I think I speak for the entire city
when I say...

00:02:03.419 --> 00:02:05.421
I love you, Big Nick!

00:02:05.421 --> 00:02:07.548
Hey, hey! This street's closed!

00:02:07.548 --> 00:02:09.216
It's the Bad Guys!

00:02:10.301 --> 00:02:11.886
Better get a move on it, Wolfie.

00:02:25.232 --> 00:02:26.901
I think we just stole Santa.

00:02:26.901 --> 00:02:28.861
Nice!

00:02:28.861 --> 00:02:31.405
The Bad Guys are stealing Big Nick!

00:02:31.405 --> 00:02:32.489
Help!

00:02:32.489 --> 00:02:34.825
-  Someone stop them!
-  Ah!

00:02:34.825 --> 00:02:36.452
That's very not good.

00:02:36.452 --> 00:02:41.332
This isn't that famous balloon everybody's
freakishly emotionally attached to, is it?

00:02:41.332 --> 00:02:44.585
No, no, no. This is a different
giant Santa-shaped balloon.

00:02:44.585 --> 00:02:46.545
- Of course it is!

00:02:51.634 --> 00:02:54.094
Whoa! Whoa! Oh!

00:02:54.094 --> 00:02:55.763
- Whoa!

00:02:57.139 --> 00:02:58.432
- Hmm?
- Huh?

00:03:03.062 --> 00:03:04.980
-  I can't see!
- Get it off of me!

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:07.441
-  The lights!
-  Santa's hugging me!

00:03:13.948 --> 00:03:15.908
Ha-ha! See ya, Santa!

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:30.381
No! Not Big Nick!

00:03:42.059 --> 00:03:46.355
Tiffany Fluffit reporting live from
the scene of the worst attack on this city

00:03:46.355 --> 00:03:48.941
since the introduction
of electric scooters.

00:03:48.941 --> 00:03:54.822
Our beloved Big Nick has been destroyed
by the notoriously notorious Bad Guys.

00:03:54.822 --> 00:03:56.865
We're a city in mourning this morning.

00:03:56.865 --> 00:03:58.492
 Why?

00:03:58.492 --> 00:04:02.162
Why indeed.
It's a senseless act of bah-humbuggery.

00:04:02.162 --> 00:04:06.375
All attempts to wash the abomination off
have only made it more terrifying,

00:04:06.375 --> 00:04:08.585
further lowering holiday spirits.

00:04:08.585 --> 00:04:11.672
It's never felt less
like Christmas in the city.

00:04:11.672 --> 00:04:12.881
Sir, your reaction?

00:04:12.881 --> 00:04:15.676
It's just not the holidays
without Big Nick.

00:04:15.676 --> 00:04:19.138
He was like a father to me.
Don't think I'll even celebrate tomorrow.

00:04:19.138 --> 00:04:22.516
<i>Probably just go into work,
guard the bank like any other day,</i>

00:04:22.516 --> 00:04:26.228
<i>and be extra attentive
to distract myself from this monstrosity.</i>

00:04:26.228 --> 00:04:27.896
<i>Why can't I look away?</i>

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:30.232
<i>You heard it here first.</i>

00:04:30.232 --> 00:04:32.318
<i>Christmas is canceled.</i>

00:04:32.318 --> 00:04:33.777
This can't be happening!

00:04:33.777 --> 00:04:35.529
The whole point of Christmas morning

00:04:35.529 --> 00:04:38.866
is that no one is around
to stop us from maximum heisting!

00:04:38.866 --> 00:04:41.452
B-b-but we were gonna rob the bank!

00:04:41.452 --> 00:04:43.912
And now we can't
because of some dumb Santa?

00:04:43.912 --> 00:04:46.332
You take that back right now!

00:04:46.332 --> 00:04:48.751
Santa is a criminal hero
who deserves our respect,

00:04:48.751 --> 00:04:50.252
in balloon form or otherwise.

00:04:50.252 --> 00:04:53.213
He's broken into more homes than anyone
and never been caught.

00:04:53.213 --> 00:04:55.507
What's even the point of anything?

00:04:55.507 --> 00:04:57.760
Unless... And hear me out on this.

00:04:57.760 --> 00:05:01.347
If we set our clocks back 24 hours
and go to sleep right now,

00:05:01.347 --> 00:05:04.266
maybe, when we wake up,
none of this will have happened.

00:05:04.266 --> 00:05:06.226
Yeah? Come on. Night, night!

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:09.897
If destroying the Santa balloon
was all it took to cancel Christmas,

00:05:09.897 --> 00:05:13.901
then all we have to do is recreate it,
and boom, Christmas is back!

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:19.073
That's the sound of
all our problems being solved,

00:05:19.073 --> 00:05:22.242
because I've already made
something better.

00:05:23.994 --> 00:05:27.039
Robo-Claus!

00:05:27.039 --> 00:05:29.833
Built this bad boy
for our Christmas morning bank job.

00:05:29.833 --> 00:05:34.046
I was gonna surprise you all tomorrow,
but you can call me a genius now.

00:05:34.046 --> 00:05:34.963
- Check it.

00:05:39.510 --> 00:05:42.721
Uh, it is surprising, for sure.

00:05:42.721 --> 00:05:45.057
The normies will forget
about their balloon

00:05:45.057 --> 00:05:47.267
once they lay their eyes on this beaut.

00:05:47.267 --> 00:05:49.311
And it captures Santa's true nature.

00:05:49.311 --> 00:05:51.188
None of that jolly business.

00:05:51.188 --> 00:05:53.607
The suit
really should be operated by a driver.

00:05:53.607 --> 00:05:54.983
Come on. Wolfie, try him on.

00:05:54.983 --> 00:05:57.736
Oh, that's... Uh, I'm good. Thanks, though.

00:05:57.736 --> 00:05:59.905
And as great as this is,

00:05:59.905 --> 00:06:03.492
the jolly component
of Jolly Old Saint Nick

00:06:03.492 --> 00:06:06.453
is probably
why non-criminal folks like him.

00:06:06.453 --> 00:06:08.622
Don't listen. You're perfect.

00:06:08.622 --> 00:06:09.832
If we all work together,

00:06:09.832 --> 00:06:14.670
I'm sure a bunch of criminal masterminds
like us can make one silly Santa balloon.

00:06:20.676 --> 00:06:22.302
Even I'm a little offended by this.

00:06:24.763 --> 00:06:26.807
His beard looks like a tentacle.

00:06:27.432 --> 00:06:28.851
I feel scandalized.

00:06:29.518 --> 00:06:32.271
Okay, lost some time there,
but we'll figure out another way

00:06:32.271 --> 00:06:34.773
to cheer up the city
in time to rob it in the morning.

00:06:34.773 --> 00:06:37.401
Which, sure, is in, like, 12 hours,
so lay it on me.

00:06:37.401 --> 00:06:39.736
What else says holiday spirit?

00:06:39.736 --> 00:06:43.866
Stealing whatever we want, because,
normally, guards take the day off.

00:06:43.866 --> 00:06:45.784
But no, not this year.

00:06:45.784 --> 00:06:48.829
They'll be at work, ruining
the only good thing about Christmas.

00:06:48.829 --> 00:06:50.247
Only good thing?

00:06:50.247 --> 00:06:53.041
What about
all the classic Christmas criminals?

00:06:53.041 --> 00:06:54.459
<i>The Grinch?</i>

00:06:54.459 --> 00:06:55.794
<i>Hans Gruber?</i>

00:06:55.794 --> 00:06:58.005
Ebenezer Scrooge!

00:06:58.005 --> 00:06:59.798
-  Ooh, nice.

00:06:59.798 --> 00:07:01.383
That guy's a legend.

00:07:01.383 --> 00:07:03.635
He parties with ghosts
and wears a dress to bed.

00:07:03.635 --> 00:07:07.639
And yet,
his story has never been properly told.

00:07:07.639 --> 00:07:11.268
So I propose that we put on a show
for the whole city,

00:07:11.268 --> 00:07:15.272
with me as Scrooge...
and all the other characters.

00:07:15.272 --> 00:07:19.985
But without that needy,
nefarious Tiny Tim tearing Scrooge down!

00:07:19.985 --> 00:07:21.862
And I would buy a ticket to that show,

00:07:21.862 --> 00:07:24.781
but we gotta stick to the awful stuff
people like--

00:07:26.700 --> 00:07:29.745
Ooh, my favorite part of the holidays
is getting a lump of coal.

00:07:29.745 --> 00:07:32.831
It really makes me feel
like I'm making good choices, you know?

00:07:32.831 --> 00:07:35.125
The Naughty List is a badge of honor.

00:07:35.125 --> 00:07:37.836
- Maybe we can get everyone some coal.
-  Piranha!

00:07:37.836 --> 00:07:39.838
- You're a genius!
- I am?

00:07:39.838 --> 00:07:43.175
- We're going to play Santa.
- No, no, no. Let me get this straight.

00:07:43.175 --> 00:07:46.929
Are you suggesting we give
instead of take?

00:07:46.929 --> 00:07:48.138
Think of it this way.

00:07:48.138 --> 00:07:50.807
We'll steal the gifts
from the big department store,

00:07:50.807 --> 00:07:53.435
and then break into houses to leave them.

00:07:53.435 --> 00:07:55.854
That sounds a lot like Robin Hood,

00:07:55.854 --> 00:07:58.315
who is notoriously good.

00:07:58.315 --> 00:08:01.151
Ugh! That guy's the worst.
He ruined tights for me.

00:08:01.151 --> 00:08:02.945
We're doing good for the greater bad.

00:08:02.945 --> 00:08:06.823
If folks have presents waiting for them,
they'll stay home on Christmas morning,

00:08:06.823 --> 00:08:09.618
and our Holiday Heist-tacular
can live again.

00:08:09.618 --> 00:08:12.788
Uh, yeah.
Uh, we also have to deal with this.

00:08:15.499 --> 00:08:17.292
After the balloon incident,

00:08:17.292 --> 00:08:20.295
the radio station
stopped playing Christmas music,

00:08:20.295 --> 00:08:25.759
and is broadcasting
something called Doom Tunes instead!

00:08:25.759 --> 00:08:27.094
- Huh?
- Huh?

00:08:27.094 --> 00:08:30.681
- Which isn't helping holiday spirit.

00:08:30.681 --> 00:08:33.517
If someone can
get into the recording studio to help,

00:08:33.517 --> 00:08:36.979
I could hack the station's antenna
and stream my sweet Santa mix.

00:08:36.979 --> 00:08:38.647
Good idea, Webs.

00:08:38.647 --> 00:08:42.526
All right, guys. Let's go do some good,
so we can be bad.

00:08:45.612 --> 00:08:46.822
Here's the plan.

00:08:46.822 --> 00:08:50.325
Piranha will help Webs get to the antenna
so she can hack it.

00:08:50.325 --> 00:08:53.245
<i>Shark will infiltrate the radio station
and distract the DJ</i>

00:08:53.245 --> 00:08:56.832
<i>so she doesn't notice Webs is
taking over the feed with holiday music.</i>

00:08:56.832 --> 00:09:00.210
<i>Finally, Snake and I will steal gifts
from the department store,</i>

00:09:00.210 --> 00:09:03.422
<i>to then break in
and leave them in unsuspecting houses.</i>

00:09:05.924 --> 00:09:11.763
And that was "No, No, No, Noel"
by Death Anchor.

00:09:11.763 --> 00:09:14.099
Bah humbug! Am I right?

00:09:15.183 --> 00:09:16.268
Scrooge?

00:09:16.268 --> 00:09:20.230
Uh, look, man, if you're here
to teach me the meaning of Christmas,

00:09:20.230 --> 00:09:21.565
I'm not interested.

00:09:22.858 --> 00:09:27.571
Don't you dare give the Right Dishonorable
Ebenezer Scrooge the horn!

00:09:27.571 --> 00:09:29.865
Buddy, I don't work with sidekicks.

00:09:29.865 --> 00:09:31.533
I kick no one's sides!

00:09:31.533 --> 00:09:33.869
Unless it's that annoying brat, Tiny Tim.

00:09:35.287 --> 00:09:36.455
This should be a breeze.

00:09:36.455 --> 00:09:39.041
All you have to do is
break into the house and leave it.

00:09:39.041 --> 00:09:41.001
Fine.

00:09:41.001 --> 00:09:42.794
Let's get this over with.

00:09:48.133 --> 00:09:50.969
Well, I definitely did it. We can go now.

00:09:53.055 --> 00:09:55.682
What? You never seen an ab before?

00:09:56.183 --> 00:09:57.184
Cough it up.

00:10:00.520 --> 00:10:01.355
Come on.

00:10:03.815 --> 00:10:06.276
Gimme a break.
Giving, not taking, is unnatural.

00:10:06.276 --> 00:10:08.320
I'll do it.

00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:10.113
Watch and learn.

00:10:14.117 --> 00:10:14.951
See?

00:10:16.203 --> 00:10:18.580
- Piece of cake.
- So, what's that, then?

00:10:18.580 --> 00:10:19.581
What's what?

00:10:25.253 --> 00:10:29.383
Get ready to sign off...
'cause I've been itching for a fight.

00:10:29.383 --> 00:10:31.968
And, you know,
you look a lot like that shark

00:10:31.968 --> 00:10:34.054
from the gang who took down Big Nick.

00:10:34.054 --> 00:10:35.555
Me? No!

00:10:35.555 --> 00:10:37.557
I am Scrooge.

00:10:37.557 --> 00:10:40.310
- See? Muttonchops?
- Ha-ha!

00:10:47.234 --> 00:10:49.486
Shark, why did you cut the station's feed?

00:10:49.486 --> 00:10:52.531
I didn't!
Well, I did, b-but she made me!

00:10:52.531 --> 00:10:55.450
Police channel's full of chatter
about the station cutting out.

00:10:55.450 --> 00:10:58.995
You got to fill the dead air before
they figure out what we're doing up here.

00:10:58.995 --> 00:11:00.706
Truly, nothing I would love more.

00:11:00.706 --> 00:11:04.751
And I do have material prepared,
but I kind of have my hands full here.

00:11:04.751 --> 00:11:06.420
-  Patch me in.

00:11:07.003 --> 00:11:09.214
You? I-I mean... you?

00:11:09.214 --> 00:11:11.508
Patch... me... in.

00:11:17.639 --> 00:11:22.310
<i>♪ This Christmas
All the bells are ringin' ♪</i>

00:11:22.811 --> 00:11:27.232
<i>♪ And the jewels are blingin' for me ♪</i>

00:11:27.232 --> 00:11:28.316
<i>♪ Ha! ♪</i>

00:11:28.316 --> 00:11:33.238
<i>♪ I'll be stealing this Christmas
You'll see ♪</i>

00:11:33.822 --> 00:11:36.450
<i>♪ It's Christmas ♪</i>

00:11:36.450 --> 00:11:42.372
<i>♪ Merry Christmas to me ♪</i>

00:11:56.803 --> 00:11:58.722
<i>Is Christmas un-canceled?</i>

00:11:58.722 --> 00:12:00.140
<i>After the unexpected carols</i>

00:12:00.140 --> 00:12:03.018
<i>and some secret Santas
leaving presents all through the city,</i>

00:12:03.018 --> 00:12:04.478
<i>holiday spirit is up.</i>

00:12:04.478 --> 00:12:08.815
<i>But is it enough to fill
the Big Nick-sized hole in our hearts?</i>

00:12:08.815 --> 00:12:10.484
<i>Stay tuned to find out.</i>

00:12:10.484 --> 00:12:12.152
Nice going, fin bro!

00:12:13.528 --> 00:12:15.071
What if it wasn't enough?

00:12:15.071 --> 00:12:18.575
If folks don't stay home to celebrate
tomorrow, we can't clean the city out.

00:12:18.575 --> 00:12:20.410
Wolfie, it's late.

00:12:20.410 --> 00:12:22.120
Look, we did the best we could.

00:12:22.120 --> 00:12:24.706
- If not this year, there's always next.
- No.

00:12:24.706 --> 00:12:27.250
We... W-we just need something big

00:12:27.250 --> 00:12:30.003
to push the holiday spirit in the city
over the edge.

00:12:30.003 --> 00:12:33.423
Oh, you can stop dropping hints now, Wolf.

00:12:33.423 --> 00:12:34.674
I'll do it.

00:12:34.674 --> 00:12:38.887
I'll perform my one-shark
Christmas villains showcase.

00:12:38.887 --> 00:12:41.681
I don't know where I'm gonna find
20 tons of fake snow,

00:12:41.681 --> 00:12:44.518
but I'm a professional, baby,
so I will find a way.

00:12:44.518 --> 00:12:45.727
Shark, that's it!

00:12:45.727 --> 00:12:48.563
If we made it snowy,
the holiday spirit would be undeniable.

00:12:48.563 --> 00:12:50.732
There would be no stopping us then.

00:12:50.732 --> 00:12:54.611
Finally, a chance to hack the atmosphere!
I actually have an app for that.

00:12:54.611 --> 00:12:57.072
We're good
with a little collateral flooding, right?

00:12:57.072 --> 00:13:01.409
Or we just steal the snow machine
at the ski resort?

00:13:01.409 --> 00:13:04.704
- We'll never get there and back in time.
-  What about that?

00:13:07.624 --> 00:13:10.710
We use the shaved ice machine
to make snow.

00:13:10.710 --> 00:13:12.712
Not as exciting
as altering Earth's weather

00:13:12.712 --> 00:13:16.800
through atmospheric geoengineering,
but I think I can make it work.

00:13:26.309 --> 00:13:28.687
Oh, thank you, thank you.
I'm all turned around.

00:13:28.687 --> 00:13:32.399
First, Christmas is canceled.
Now, maybe it's back on.

00:13:32.399 --> 00:13:33.942
So I rebuy everything.

00:13:33.942 --> 00:13:35.986
W-what flavor can I get you?

00:13:35.986 --> 00:13:38.321
Uh, please describe them to me
in great detail

00:13:38.321 --> 00:13:41.157
while I interrupt
with all sorts of unnecessary questions.

00:13:43.577 --> 00:13:44.578
Aha.

00:13:45.245 --> 00:13:46.246
Hmm.

00:13:46.955 --> 00:13:50.625
Does Mistletoe Mint
taste more like missiles or toes?

00:13:50.625 --> 00:13:51.751
It tastes like mint.

00:13:54.129 --> 00:13:57.966
Please maintain eye contact
with me at all times!

00:13:57.966 --> 00:13:59.342
Oh, wait. Well, I...

00:13:59.342 --> 00:14:03.179
I require trustworthiness
from all my frozen-delicacy suppliers.

00:14:03.179 --> 00:14:05.849
When I give you the signal,
turn the dial up.

00:14:05.849 --> 00:14:06.933
A five should do it.

00:14:11.938 --> 00:14:13.398
- All set, Wolfie.

00:14:13.398 --> 00:14:14.816
<i>Fire her up.</i>

00:14:17.277 --> 00:14:21.156
Nothing's gonna get in the way
of our Holiday Heist-tacular.

00:14:28.038 --> 00:14:29.247
Hmm?

00:14:29.247 --> 00:14:30.165
Huh?

00:14:30.165 --> 00:14:31.499
-  Ooh!

00:14:37.505 --> 00:14:38.965
Tiffany Fluffit reporting live

00:14:38.965 --> 00:14:42.093
from the scene of
an unexpected winter wonderland.

00:14:42.093 --> 00:14:44.512
It may not be real,
but what in this town is?

00:14:44.512 --> 00:14:47.766
In fact, it's never felt more
like the holidays in the city.

00:14:47.766 --> 00:14:50.310
Christmas is officially back on!

00:14:54.147 --> 00:14:55.774
It's beautiful!

00:14:55.774 --> 00:14:57.442
We did it. We really did it.

00:14:57.442 --> 00:14:59.569
It makes me feel all warm inside.

00:14:59.569 --> 00:15:01.780
So merry and b-bright,

00:15:01.780 --> 00:15:05.033
like someone lit a candle
in the cold cavern of my heart.

00:15:05.867 --> 00:15:09.871
If you like that sort of thing.
Which I don't. I do not.

00:15:19.047 --> 00:15:21.007
She's gonna blow!

00:15:23.093 --> 00:15:25.053
That psychic was right!

00:15:25.637 --> 00:15:27.597
That's not good.

00:15:27.597 --> 00:15:29.265
It's too cold!

00:15:39.693 --> 00:15:43.196
For a brief moment,
it looked like the holidays were back on,

00:15:43.196 --> 00:15:45.115
but that moment has passed.

00:15:45.115 --> 00:15:48.702
A frozen vortex
is spinning out of control downtown.

00:15:48.702 --> 00:15:51.246
Will it suck in all surrounding life?

00:15:52.956 --> 00:15:55.542
That's not going to happen.

00:15:55.542 --> 00:15:56.710
Probably.

00:15:56.710 --> 00:16:00.422
As long as you didn't turn the dial
all the way up. Wolf?

00:16:00.422 --> 00:16:03.174
I-I figured a ten
would be twice the holiday spirit?

00:16:03.174 --> 00:16:04.342
- What?
- Why, I ought to...

00:16:04.342 --> 00:16:07.470
- You're lucky my fins are frozen!
- I'm too talented to die!

00:16:07.470 --> 00:16:10.598
That vortex is about to suck in the city!
No time to be mad at me!

00:16:10.598 --> 00:16:13.018
I'll make time. Everything was fine.

00:16:13.018 --> 00:16:15.895
But no, you had to go
and push things too far,

00:16:15.895 --> 00:16:17.772
like always!

00:16:19.065 --> 00:16:20.608
I know. I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

00:16:20.608 --> 00:16:23.820
It's just, stealing with you all
Christmas morning

00:16:23.820 --> 00:16:25.488
is the highlight of my year.

00:16:25.488 --> 00:16:29.034
I got so wrapped up in making sure
our Holiday Heist-tacular happened

00:16:29.034 --> 00:16:30.285
that I put you at risk.

00:16:30.285 --> 00:16:33.580
And that's the last thing
I'd ever want to do.

00:16:35.540 --> 00:16:36.458
Uh...

00:16:36.458 --> 00:16:38.293
- Yo, get a life.
- That's gross.

00:16:38.293 --> 00:16:41.504
- These are theatrical tears.
- Yeah, fine, whatever.

00:16:41.504 --> 00:16:42.797
Better stop that machine,

00:16:42.797 --> 00:16:45.967
or it won't just be
our Holiday Heist-tacular that's canceled.

00:16:45.967 --> 00:16:48.344
Webs, can't you, like, hack your device?

00:16:48.344 --> 00:16:51.514
Oh, yeah, sure.
Why didn't I think of that?

00:16:51.514 --> 00:16:53.516
Of course I can't hack it!

00:16:53.516 --> 00:16:55.894
Think I'd leave security loopholes
in my own tech?

00:16:55.894 --> 00:16:58.354
The only way to stop it is to unplug it.

00:16:59.272 --> 00:17:00.899
Then that's what we do.

00:17:15.288 --> 00:17:16.623
Fin bro!

00:17:22.545 --> 00:17:24.839
Cover your eyes! Don't look at me!

00:17:26.883 --> 00:17:28.843
If Shark's not strong enough, who is?

00:17:29.928 --> 00:17:31.429
I know who.

00:17:34.516 --> 00:17:36.309
The situation has worsened.

00:17:36.309 --> 00:17:38.144
- Oh!

00:17:43.191 --> 00:17:46.027
- Are you seeing this?

00:17:49.739 --> 00:17:51.116
 Not that way! How do I...

00:17:51.699 --> 00:17:54.744
<i>Ah, you have to relax.
The suit is intuitive.</i>

00:17:54.744 --> 00:17:56.121
Don't force it.

00:17:56.121 --> 00:17:57.539
<i>Just walk.</i>

00:18:17.684 --> 00:18:21.604
Whoa! Folks, we're witnessing
some sort of Christmas miracle.

00:18:21.604 --> 00:18:25.275
A Santa cyborg
appears to be attempting to save the city!

00:18:33.074 --> 00:18:34.951
Whoa!

00:18:39.539 --> 00:18:40.623
Whoa!

00:18:40.623 --> 00:18:43.376
- I got you!

00:19:30.465 --> 00:19:33.218
One at a time, folks. Please, form a line.

00:19:35.053 --> 00:19:36.054
Whoa! Whoa!

00:19:42.227 --> 00:19:47.565
Balloon Santa may have gone up in flames,
but the city has a new Santa mascot.

00:19:47.565 --> 00:19:52.987
That's right, Robo-Claus is
a huge mech robot that screams family fun.

00:19:54.614 --> 00:19:57.575
Well, I gotta hand it to you, Webs,
they really love your Santa.

00:19:57.575 --> 00:19:58.952
Maybe too much.

00:19:58.952 --> 00:20:02.705
These people gotta get home if we're
to pull our morning Holiday Heist-tacular.

00:20:02.705 --> 00:20:03.748
Ah.

00:20:13.883 --> 00:20:16.094
Shark, I patched your comms into the suit.

00:20:16.094 --> 00:20:18.930
He's no Scrooge,
but think you could play Santa?

00:20:18.930 --> 00:20:22.767
Ho-ho-ho-ho-ho! Happy Holidays!

00:20:22.767 --> 00:20:24.644
Now, it's late,

00:20:24.644 --> 00:20:26.688
so everyone go to bed,

00:20:26.688 --> 00:20:32.193
because Santa commands that everyone
celebrate tomorrow in their homes,

00:20:32.193 --> 00:20:34.570
and not at their security guard jobs.

00:20:34.570 --> 00:20:36.197
<i>- Ho-ho-ho!</i>
- I'll do it.

00:20:36.197 --> 00:20:38.825
I'll stay home for you, Robo-Claus.

00:20:38.825 --> 00:20:40.243
Please be proud of me.

00:20:40.868 --> 00:20:41.995
We did it!

00:20:43.079 --> 00:20:46.541
- The Bad Guys saved Christ--

00:20:51.421 --> 00:20:54.882
I can't believe that,
after all that, we're too si--

00:20:56.009 --> 00:20:59.220
...we're too sick
to pull off our Holiday Heist-tacular.

00:20:59.220 --> 00:21:01.806
How about a new holiday tradition?

00:21:01.806 --> 00:21:04.434
No more traditions or holidays.

00:21:04.434 --> 00:21:06.811
Bah hu--

00:21:08.187 --> 00:21:11.482
What... is... that?

00:21:13.234 --> 00:21:15.320
Oh, no. I think they're presents.

00:21:15.320 --> 00:21:16.362
Like, for us?

00:21:16.362 --> 00:21:20.033
Must have done so much good for the city
that we ended up on Santa's Nice List.

00:21:20.033 --> 00:21:22.160
I'm gonna be sick!

00:21:22.994 --> 00:21:24.495
The shame!

00:21:24.495 --> 00:21:28.791
Not only did that bearded freak
have the gall to break into our lair,

00:21:28.791 --> 00:21:32.295
he goes and gives us presents, not coal!

00:21:33.338 --> 00:21:36.382
Wait. Is that stinky cheese?
How did he know?

00:21:36.382 --> 00:21:39.552
The Bad Guys will be the laughing stock
of the criminal community.

00:21:39.552 --> 00:21:42.138
I'll never be able to show my face again.

00:21:42.138 --> 00:21:43.890
This will not stand.

00:21:43.890 --> 00:21:45.641
We need to start planning now.

00:21:45.641 --> 00:21:48.102
Next year,
we are going to heist the North Pole

00:21:48.102 --> 00:21:51.731
and show Santa that the Bad Guys
belong on the Naughty List.

00:21:53.232 --> 00:21:54.275
<i>And so, yeah</i>

00:21:54.275 --> 00:21:56.986
<i>The Bad Guys stole Christmas
From ourselves</i>

00:21:56.986 --> 00:21:59.614
<i>And Santa deemed us good little elves</i>

00:21:59.614 --> 00:22:02.825
<i>Until next year, when we get all not nice</i>

00:22:02.825 --> 00:22:06.496
<i>Happy Heisting to all
And to all, a good heist</i>
